d_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":10,"created_at":"2026-06-25T12:14:27Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T13:15:58Z","closed_at":"2026-09-04T13:14:45Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nThe problem started in version 4.7 with the addition of the joystick \n\n### System information\n\n4.7.stable on Android \n\n### Issue description\n\nIn Godot 4.7 stable on Android, UI elements (like touch joysticks) misalign when launching the game. The joystick is placed on the right side in the editor canvas, but shifts to the left side inside the built-in preview window. (Screenshots attached below)\n\n\n<img width=\"2400\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a4805fc1-0b9c-4193-8464-013e6be947b7\" />\n<img width=\"2400\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/44f0c0d9-f4a6-46e4-b62a-4b1b1807e0c8\" />\n<img width=\"2400\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c5393972-5606-46c1-a0fa-8696c7bbcc9f\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Open Godot 4.7 on Android.\n2. Place a touch control on one side of the screen (e.g., right side).\n3. Launch the game in the built-in preview window.\n4. Notice that the layout is completely mirrored/reversed (if placed on the right, it shifts to the left, and vice versa).\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A (Screenshots attached)","close